Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

ISOLATED ZERO WM RENDERER CHECKS

Run from any directory:
  bash /path/to/zero-foundation/review-tests/wm-renderer/run.sh

Requires the built own compiler at build/zero, host Python3 and ImageMagick
convert. Python is external test orchestration and the independent reference
oracle; it is never compiled into the OS. All actual drawing is the production
wm/worker.zero.part compiled to native machine code by Zero.

The .zero.part fixtures provide a hosted guarded framebuffer and test rings.
The script substitutes a bounded outer loop and removes context switches to
isolate drawing. It writes complete generated Zero test sources, executables
and PPM intermediates to a fresh build/wm-renderer.* directory. Evidence and
PNG fixture previews go to verification/wm-renderer-0.8.0.

The suite verifies framebuffer guards, nontrivial stride padding, RGB/BGR
agreement, compact layouts and9 terminal-replay cases. It does not claim to
exercise generation changes across a real yield, guest input, page allocation,
BIOS/UEFI handoff, filesystem behavior or lifecycle scheduling.
No user data disk is opened. No VM is started by this suite.
